const FOUNDATION = args.foundationReport || "### ui-kit\nI finished the design-system kit: every primitive from ARCHITECTURE.md \u00a76 now exists, plus the tab bar, status header, `<UiShowcase/>` and `docs/COMPONENTS.md`. The whole project typechecks with 0 errors, lint is clean on my folders, and the showcase bundles with Metro for both iOS and web.\n\n**How I checked it.** Nothing was running on port 8081 and I didn't start the Expo dev server. There's also no `/dev` route yet, because `src/app` belongs to the shell agent. Instead I bundled the showcase for web through a throwaway entry file in my folder, deleted it straight after, served the bundle from the scratchpad on port 8799 with a plain file server, and went through every group at phone and tablet widths. That review found and fixed:\n- **Accessibility on web:** react-native-web ignores `accessibilityState`, so selected/checked/disabled states never reached the page. `PressableScale` now passes them as `aria-*` props, which work on iOS, Android and web. `accessibilityElementsHidden` is replaced by `aria-hidden`.\n- **Chat composer on web:** it opened two rows tall and showed the browser's orange focus ring. It now starts at one row, grows with the text, and the pill corners stay round as it grows.\n- **`StatTile`:** values sat at different heights depending on the icon type; they now line up.\n- **`Tag`:** the default butter pill was nearly invisible on white cards. It now uses the stronger amber background, like the video's yellow pill.\n- **`ListItem`:** a row with a `Switch` hid the switch from screen readers; fixed.\n\nThe browser pane was hidden while I tested, so it slowed animation frames to almost nothing. Final layouts are verified, but animation timing is not. That covers entrances, the sheet slide, the tab pill spring, confetti and the chip bump. It still needs a check on a device or a visible browser.\n\n**Files created this run**\n- **ui:** `radio.tsx`, `choice-row.tsx`, `switch.tsx`, `text-field.tsx`, `skeleton.tsx`, `empty-state.tsx`, `count-up.tsx`, `stat-tile.tsx`, `screen-title.tsx`, barrel `index.ts`, `showcase.tsx` and `showcase-parts/` (7 section files plus a layout helper).\n- **navigation:** `floating-tab-bar.tsx`, `tab-bar-item.tsx`, `tab-config.ts`, `status-header.tsx`, barrel `index.ts`.\n- **docs:** `docs/COMPONENTS.md`.\n- **Kept from the interrupted run, with the fixes above:** text, pressable-scale, button, icon-button, card, spotlight, chip, stat-chip, rolling-number, tag, badge, progress-bar, segmented-progress, list-item, list-group, section-header, icon-tile, avatar, divider, stack, screen, sheet, dialog, dialog-badge, toast, typing-dots, shimmer, confetti, motion-presets, use-reduce-motion, tones, icon, metrics, `lib/haptics.ts`, `lib/platform.ts`.\n- **Removed:** an empty leftover `ui/showcase/` folder.\n\n**Public API**\n- **From `@/components/ui`:**\n  - **Text & layout:** `Text`, `AnimatedText`, `useTextStyle`, `Icon`, `renderIcon`, `VStack`, `HStack`, `Spacer`, `Divider`, `Screen`, `ScreenTitle`, `SectionHeader`.\n  - **Actions & surfaces:** `PressableScale`, `Button`, `IconButton`, `Card`, `Spotlight`, `ListItem` / `MenuRow`, `ListGroup`, `IconTile` / `EmojiTile`, `Avatar`, `StoryRing`, `StatTile`, `EmptyState`.\n  - **Indicators & progress:** `Chip`, `StatChip`, `Tag`, `Badge`, `RollingNumber`, `CountUp`, `ProgressBar`, `SegmentedProgress`, `Skeleton`, `SkeletonText`, `TypingDots`.\n  - **Inputs & overlays:** `TextField`, `Radio`, `ChoiceRow`, `Switch`, `Sheet`, `Dialog`, `DialogBadge`, `ToastHost`, `toast`, `useToast`.\n  - **Motion & helpers:** `Shimmer`, `Confetti`, `useShake`, `useBump`, `bumpAnimation`, `shakeAnimation`, `popAnimation`, `feedbackMotion`, `useReduceMotion`, `setReduceMotionOverride`, `resolveTone`, and the control sizes (`controlHeight`, `iconSize`, `avatarSize`, \u2026).\n- **From `@/components/navigation`:** `FloatingTabBar`, `StatusHeader`, `TAB_CONFIG`, `getTabConfig`, `useTabBarInset`, `getTabBarInset`, `getTabBarBottomOffset`.\n- **Libs:** `@/lib/haptics` (`haptics.*`, `triggerHaptic`, `setHapticsEnabled`) and `@/lib/platform` (`isWeb`, `isIOS`, `isAndroid`, `isNative`, `platformSelect`).\n- **Dev only:** `UiShowcase` from `@/components/ui/showcase`, props `toastHost` (default true) and `withTabBar`.\n- Full props and usage examples for everything are in `docs/COMPONENTS.md`.\n\n**Token additions:** none in `src/theme/tokens/*`. I appended control sizes (`switchSize`, `skeletonLine`, `readableWidth`) to `ui/metrics.ts`, which is in my folder.\n\n**Known gaps**\n- **Shell wiring still needed:**\n  - `(tabs)/_layout.tsx` with `FloatingTabBar`.\n  - A connected `StatusHeader`.\n  - `<ToastHost toast={useUi(s => s.toast)} onHide={useUi(s => s.hideToast)} />` at the root; I added this controlled mode so it reads the store's toasts.\n  - Calls to `setHapticsEnabled` and `setReduceMotionOverride` from the user's settings.\n  - A `/dev` route rendering `<UiShowcase/>`.\n- **Toasts under overlays:** on native, a toast renders underneath an open Sheet or Dialog.\n- **Web composer shrink:** the multiline field only shrinks back when it is cleared, not while the user deletes text.\n- **Template leftover:** `ui/collapsible.tsx` is still there because the template's `explore.tsx` imports it. It isn't part of the kit or the barrel.\n- **Lesson answer tiles:** graded answer options with correct/wrong states belong to the lesson feature, as noted in the docs.\n- No npm packages are needed.\n\nMain files:\n- /Users/sami/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/ff5c0b24-8b45-4a60-8168-828b5622921e/346a4904-d962-464e-a954-66c144faa0ee/scratch-2026-09-29-4e59a3/finanz/docs/COMPONENTS.md\n- /Users/sami/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/ff5c0b24-8b45-4a60-8168-828b5622921e/346a4904-d962-464e-a954-66c144faa0ee/scratch-2026-09-29-4e59a3/finanz/src/components/ui/index.ts\n- /Users/sami/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/ff5c0b24-8b45-4a60-8168-828b5622921e/346a4904-d962-464e-a954-66c144faa0ee/scratch-2026-09-29-4e59a3/finanz/src/components/ui/sho\n\u2026(truncated; read the code/docs for the rest)\n\n### icons-illustrations\nEverything in the icon and illustration set is now done: all 14 icons, a renderer that covers every `IllustrationKey` in `src/content/types.ts`, all the named compositions you listed, both barrel files and both galleries. `tsc --noEmit` shows 0 errors in the two folders (0 project-wide), and `eslint` passes on both. I also rendered every piece, and both galleries, to PNG at several sizes on paper and on evergreen to check them by eye. I didn't open the galleries inside the app, because no route mounts them and routes are outside my folders.\n\nPaths below are relative to `/Users/sami/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/ff5c0b24-8b45-4a60-8168-828b5622921e/346a4904-d962-464e-a954-66c144faa0ee/scratch-2026-09-29-4e59a3/finanz/src/components/`.\n\n**Kept from the interrupted run (checked visually)**\n- **Icons:** flame, heart, heart with \u221e, kiwi coin (seeds simplified below 24px), shield, gem, trophy, lock, sparkle, gift, bolt, check badge, cross badge, `FinanzLogo`, `FinanzWordmark`.\n- **Illustrations:** `HeroBookSpotlight`, `ReferralEnvelopes`, `KiwiPattern`, the four course covers and the 11 lesson spot illustrations.\n\n**Created this run**\n- `icons/lib/trophy-shape.tsx`: the trophy drawing, now shared by `TrophyIcon` (refactored to use it) and `TrophyCups`.\n- `icons/lib/gallery-kit.tsx`: layout pieces shared by the two galleries.\n- `icons/gallery.tsx`: `IconGallery`.\n- `illustrations/lib/place.ts`: small helper for positioning icon-grid artwork.\n- `illustrations/economy/`: `streak-flame-hero.tsx`, `shield-pair.tsx`, `hearts-trio.tsx`, `trophy-cups.tsx`.\n- `illustrations/assistant-orb.tsx`, `illustrations/empty-box.tsx`.\n- `illustrations/illustration.tsx`: the registry.\n- `illustrations/index.ts`: barrel.\n- `illustrations/gallery.tsx`: `IllustrationGallery`.\n\n**Edited this run**\n- `ShieldDetails` got a `chevron?: boolean` prop.\n- `compound-snowball-art`: the hill is now a rounded slope that fades out, instead of a hard-edged wedge.\n- `stocks-cover`: the red candles read as \"+\" signs, so I gave them taller bodies.\n- Artboard sizes are now exported as constants from the files that have their own size.\n\n**Public API**\n- **Icons** (`@/components/icons`): every icon takes `{ size?: number = 24; muted?: boolean; style?; accessibilityLabel? }`. Extras:\n  - `LockIcon`: `variant?: 'grey' | 'gold'`.\n  - `SparkleIcon`: `tone?: 'white' | 'lime' | 'gold' | 'brand'`, `twin?: boolean`.\n  - `FinanzLogo`: `tone?: 'lime' | 'brand'` (no `muted`).\n  - `FinanzWordmark`: `{ height?, tone?: 'ink' | 'white' | 'lime', withMark?, style? }`.\n  - Also exported: `FzMonogram`, `IconProps`.\n- **Illustrations** (`@/components/illustrations`): everything takes `{ width?, height?, style?, accessibilityLabel? }`. If only `width` is given, height follows the artwork's proportions.\n  - `<Illustration name={IllustrationKey} background?: 'brand' | 'paper' />`. `background` only affects course covers.\n  - `ILLUSTRATION_KEYS` lists every key; `illustrationSize(name)` returns the natural `[width, height]`.\n  - Keys mapped to named compositions: `trophy` \u2192 `TrophyCups`, `shield` \u2192 `ShieldPair`, `envelopes` \u2192 `ReferralEnvelopes`, `kiwi-pattern` \u2192 `KiwiPattern`.\n  - Course covers fill their box and crop (`xMidYMid slice`); `KiwiPattern` does too. Everything else keeps its proportions inside the box.\n  - `CourseCover { variant, background? }`, `COURSE_COVERS`, `isCourseCoverKey`, the four cover components and the 11 `*Art` components are also exported.\n  - `KiwiPattern { density?: 'sparse' | 'regular' | 'dense'; mode?: 'vivid' | 'ghost' | 'tint' }`.\n  - `StreakFlameHero { tone?: 'ghost' | 'vivid' }`: defaults to `ghost`, a faint lime flame for the evergreen streak header. `vivid` is full colour with glow and embers.\n  - `ShieldPair { muted? }`: the front shield carries the streak flame.\n  - `HeartsTrio { filled?: 0\u20133; variant?: 'rose' | 'gold' }`: hearts beyond `filled` render grey, filling left \u2192 centre \u2192 right.\n  - `TrophyCups { muted? }`: two cups toasting, with confetti. `muted` gives a grey, uncelebrated version for courses not yet finished.\n  - `AssistantOrb { halo? }`: static pearl; the assistant screen should animate a wrapper around it.\n  - `EmptyBox`: empty-state box.\n- **Galleries:**\n  - `IconGallery { sizes?: [48, 20], scrollable? }` from `@/components/icons/gallery`.\n  - `IllustrationGallery { widths?: [176, 88], surface?: 'paper' | 'evergreen', scrollable? }` from `@/components/illustrations/gallery`.\n  - They are kept out of the barrels. Both render on paper and on evergreen; the icon gallery also has a muted section and the wordmarks.\n\n**Tokens:** I added none this run. The set uses `illustration.mutedLight`, `mutedDeep` and `blushDeep`, which are already appended in `src/theme/tokens/colors.ts`. They were most likely added by the interrupted run, but I couldn't confirm that from the logs.\n\n**Known gaps**\n- **Lesson art on dark backgrounds:** the 11 spot illustrations are tuned for light cards. On evergreen, the evergreen outlines lose contrast (cart frame and wheels, scale stand, phone body), so use them on paper.\n- **Background-specific pieces:** `SparkleIcon tone=\"brand\"` and `FinanzLogo tone=\"brand\"` are for light surfaces, and `StreakFlameHero` in its default `ghost` tone is for evergreen. Each is nearly invisible on the other background.\n- **Galleries need a screen:** nothing mounts them yet. Someone who owns `src/app` needs to add a dev route, for example `<IconGallery scrollable />`.\n- **No new packages were needed.**\n\n### content\nI've written all the static content: 13 Italian lessons, courses, stories, shop and an offline assistant knowledge base. The project typechecks with 0 errors, and my validation script passes on every check. I couldn't run `expo lint`: eslint isn't installed and `expo lint` would install packages, which the task rules out. No theme tokens were added.\n\n**Files created** (all under `src/content/`, none over 261 lines; `types.ts` is untouched):\n- `index.ts` \u2014 a single entry point that re-exports everything below, so screens can `import \u2026 from '@/content'`.\n- `extra-types.ts` \u2014 new types that aren't in the contract (see the last section).\n- `courses.ts`\n- `lessons/index.ts`, `lessons/answer-label.ts`, and one file per chapter: `inflazione`, `interesse-composto`, `rischi-rendimenti`, `azioni`, `dividendi`, `capital-gain`, `obbligazioni`, `cedole`, `etf`, `diversifica`, `broker`, `scegli-broker`, `dentro-broker`.\n- `stories.ts`, `shop.ts`, `challenges.ts`\n- `assistant.ts`, plus `assistant-kb/{index,basics,markets,practice,app}.ts`\n\n**Public API:**\n- **`courses.ts`:** `MAIN_COURSE_ID`, `COURSES`, `CHAPTERS`, and helpers `getCourse`, `getChapter`, `getCourseForChapter`, `getLevelForChapter`, `orderedChapterIds`, `orderedChapters`, `getNextChapterId`, `chapterCount` (13 for the main course, a planned number for coming-soon courses) and `courseRewards` (340 XP / 420 coins in total). Lookups return `undefined` for unknown ids.\n- **`lessons/index.ts`:** `LESSONS`, `getLesson(id): Lesson` (throws on an unknown id), `findLesson` (returns `undefined` instead; use it in routes), `hasLesson`, `getStep`, `gradedStepCount`, and `getCorrectAnswerLabel(step)`, which gives the right answer as text (true/false, a match list or an ordered list).\n- **`stories.ts`:** `STORY_GROUPS`, `getStoryGroup`, `storyGroupIndex`, `STORY_BRAND_MARK = 'FZ'` and `POLL_CARD_TITLE = 'Piccolo sondaggio'`.\n- **`shop.ts`:** `SHOP_ITEMS` (the unlimited-hour item's `amount` is 60 minutes), `SHOP_ITEM_DESCRIPTIONS`, `getShopItem`, `MILESTONES` (2 lessons \u2192 1 shield, 10 \u2192 1000 coins, 15 \u2192 7 days of Pro), `milestoneLockedLabel(n)` (\"Sblocca dopo n lezioni\"), `PRO_PLAN` (6,99\u20ac a month or 49,99\u20ac a year, prices in cents, clearly marked as a demo) and `REFERRAL_PROMO`.\n- **`challenges.ts`:** `MARATHON_CHALLENGES` (7 days \u2192 +500, and a second challenge that unlocks at a 14-day streak).\n- **`assistant.ts`:**\n  - Constants: `ASSISTANT_GREETING`, `SUGGESTED_PROMPTS` (6 plain strings), `ASSISTANT_DISCLAIMER`, `ASSISTANT_FALLBACK`, `ASSISTANT_INPUT_PLACEHOLDER`, `ASSISTANT_NAME`, `EXPLAIN_MISTAKE_REQUEST`, `EXPLAIN_STEP_REQUEST`.\n  - Knowledge base: `ASSISTANT_KB` has 36 entries. It covers every topic in the course, plus a rule that answers requests for personal advice with a polite refusal, and small talk.\n  - Helpers: `answerQuestion(text)`, `findKbEntry`, `getKbEntry`, `normalizeQuery`, `explainMistake(stepExplanation, correctLabel)` and `explainStep(explanation)` for the \u2728 button on steps that aren't graded.\n\n**Content facts:**\n- Every lesson has 9 steps (10 for Dentro un broker), with 5 graded steps of at least 2 different types. Every step has an `explanation`, so the \u2728 button also has something to show on info and definition steps. All text is within the length limits.\n- Inflazione steps 1\u20135 match the video. The added steps are: fill on \"potere d'acquisto\", a choice where the answer is \"Circa 971\u20ac\" (1.000 \u00f7 1,03 \u2248 970,87\u20ac), a match, and a closing \"Come difendersi\" pointing to Interesse composto.\n- All numbers were checked, e.g. 1.000\u20ac at 5% gives 1.102,50\u20ac after 2 years and \u22481.628,89\u20ac after 10.\n- Tax figures: 26%, 12,5% on government bonds, and 0,20% stamp duty.\n- I spread the correct option across first, middle and last positions so users can't guess by position.\n\n**Choices that differ from the spec:**\n- I used typographic \u2019 and \u2026 throughout, and the correct spelling \"perch\u00e9\" in my constants, where the video writes \"perch\u00e8\". Screens that hardcode the video's spelling won't match.\n- The video's \"CHI SIAMO ??\" is written `'CHI SIAMO??'`.\n- The FZ logo card uses `emoji: STORY_BRAND_MARK`. If rendered as plain text it shows \"FZ\"; the story viewer should draw the logo tile instead.\n\n**Known gaps:**\n- The 15-lesson milestone can't be reached with the 13 chapters unless the store counts replays or future courses.\n- Choice and fill options come in a fixed order; order steps list items in the correct order, so the UI must shuffle them.\n- The 33% tax rate on crypto gains from 2026 comes from my knowledge of the 2025 Budget Law and wasn't checked against a live source. It's worth re-checking before release.\n\n**New types:** `types.ts` needed no new fields. What wasn't in it lives in `extra-types.ts`: `Milestone`, `MilestoneReward`, `MarathonChallenge`, `ProPlan`, `ProBenefit`, `ProBenefitIcon`, `ProPrice`, `ReferralPromo`, `AssistantKbEntry` and `AssistantReply`.\n\nThe validator can be re-run: `\u2026/scratchpad/content-check/validate.js`, after compiling `src/content` into `content-check/build` with tsc.\n\n### store-logic\nI've built the app state and the lesson logic as specified in ARCHITECTURE.md \u00a74 and \u00a77. The typecheck reports 0 errors across the whole project, with no unused code in my files. All 16 scratchpad tests pass in three time zones, and every one of the 13 real lessons plays through the lesson machine to 100%. Lint was not run, and the running dev server hasn't loaded any of my files yet (see Known gaps).\n\n**Files created** (all under `finanz/src`)\n- `store/index.ts`: the one persisted store. `persist(createJSONStorage(AsyncStorage))`, `name: 'finanz-store'`, `version: 1`. Saved state includes only data fields, never actions or `_hasHydrated`. Old saved data is cleaned when loaded: wrong-typed values are dropped and new settings get their defaults. When loading finishes, lives and streak are synced and `setHasHydrated(true)` runs, even if loading failed.\n- `store/types.ts`, `constants.ts`, `initial-state.ts` (the demo user Alberto, as specified).\n- `store/storage.ts`: storage, save-filter, merge and migration logic, plus an inert storage for the web static render.\n- `store/slices/{profile,economy,progress,meta}.ts`, each typed `StateCreator<RootState, [], [], Slice>`.\n- `store/rules/{lives,streak,levels,shop,progress}.ts`: pure rule functions.\n- `store/milestones.ts`, `store/challenges.ts`: progress for Home milestones and \"Sfide Maratona\".\n- `store/selectors.ts`, `store/hooks.ts`, `store/ui.ts`.\n- `lib/dates.ts`, `lib/format.ts`, `lib/random.ts`.\n- `features/lesson/machine.ts`, `machine.types.ts`.\n\n**Public API**\n- **Store:** `useStore`, `useStoreShallow(selector)`, `getStoreState`, `subscribeStore`, `syncTimeBasedState(now)`, `resetStore()`. `index.ts` also re-exports the selectors, constants and rule functions.\n- **Economy:** `spend(n): boolean`, `earn(n)`, `loseLife(now): boolean`, `syncLives(now): number`, `addLives(n, now)`, `activateUnlimited(min, now)`, `activatePro(days, now)`, `addShields(n)`, `buy(itemId, now)`, `claimDailyReward(now)`. `buy` returns `{ok:true} | {ok:false, reason:'insufficient-coins'|'already-claimed'|'lives-full'}`.\n- **Lives:** the pure `computeLives(state, now)` returns `{lives, nextRefillAt, fullAt, isFull, \u2026}`. One life comes back every 2 hours; losing a life while already below max doesn't restart the clock.\n- **Progress:** `startOrResumeSession`, `saveSessionStep(chapterId, stepIndex, lostLifeStepIds, mistakeStepIds?)`, `clearSession`, `completeChapter({chapterId, accuracy, xp, coins, now})` \u2192 `{xpEarned, coinsEarned, accuracy, isFirstCompletion, streakBefore, streakAfter, isNewStreakDay, milestoneReached?}`. Also `syncStreak(now)`, `claimMilestone(id, now)` and `claimChallenge(id, now)`.\n- **Other actions:** profile (`updateProfile`, `setInterests`, `toggleInterest`, `completeOnboarding`, `setLanguage`, `addInvitedFriend`) and meta (`markStorySeen`, `answerPoll`, `setSetting`, `markReferralPromoShown`, `resetAll`).\n- **Selectors:** every selector takes `(state, \u2026args)`, e.g. `selectCurrentChapter(state, courseId)`. Beyond your list I added `selectStreakInfo`, `selectLongestStreak`, `selectChallenges`, `selectLives`, `selectCanLoseLife(s, chapterId, now)`, `selectIsOutOfLives`, `selectShopItemState`, `selectReferralPromoDue` and `selectChapterStatuses`.\n- **Streak rule:** a shield bridges one missed day only, and only when that day is yesterday and the day before was active. Two missed days in a row always break the streak. A shield bought today cannot bring back an older lost streak.\n- **Hooks (`@/store/hooks`):** `useHasHydrated`, `useNow(ms)`, `useSyncTimeBasedState()` (mount once in the root layout), `useLives`, `useStreakInfo`, `useCourseProgress`, `useChapterStatuses`, `useResumeInfo`, `useMilestones`, `useChallenges`, `useUserLevel`. Selectors that return objects make a new value on every call, so in components use these hooks or `useStoreShallow` to avoid re-render loops.\n- **`useUi`:** `sheet` (one of `lives`, `out-of-lives`, `referral`, `rate`, `redeem`, `shield-info`), `openSheet`, `closeSheet`, `toast`, `showToast`, `hideToast(id)`, `sessionFlags`, `setSessionFlag`.\n- **Lesson machine:** `transition(state, event, steps)` returns `{state, effects}`. Events are `SELECT`, `CHECK`, `MATCH_MISS` (a wrong pair in the pair-by-pair match UI), `RETRY`, `NEXT`, `RESTORE`. Effects are `LOSE_LIFE`, `FEEDBACK`, `PERSIST_PROGRESS` and `COMPLETED`.\n- **Lesson helpers:** `createLessonState`, `reduceLesson`, `isAnswerComplete`, `gradeStep`, `checkPair`, `isStepGraded`, `computeAccuracy`, `shouldLoseLife`, `getPrimaryAction`, `getLessonProgress`, `TRUE_FALSE_OPTION_IDS`. Match answers map left pair id to right pair id; order answers are a list of item ids.\n- **Formatting and random:** `formatCoins` ('1.000'), `formatEuro`, `formatPercent`, `pluralize`, `formatLessons`, `formatCountdown` ('2h 26min'), `formatCountdownClock`. `getMonthMatrix(year, month0)` gives the Monday-first 6\u00d77 calendar grid, and `shuffle(items, seed)` / `shuffleUnsolved` give stable shuffles.\n\n**Token additions:** none.\n\n**Behaviour choices you may want to revisit**\n- \"Lessons completed\" counts replays. The content file notes that the 15-lesson milestone can't be reached otherwise, since the course has 13 chapters. `selectChaptersCompleted` gives the distinct count.\n- Unlimited lives and Pro both refill lives to max when activated, and unlimited hours stack.\n- Buying the unlimited hour while Pro is active returns `lives-full`.\n- `buy()` throws on an unknown item id.\n- Replaying a completed chapter never costs a life. `computeChapterReward` suggests half XP and no coins for replays.\n- The daily reward is not recorded in purchase history.\n\n**Known gaps**\n- **The running dev server can't see new files.** Metro on port 8081 returns 404 for any file created after it started (my store, `src/theme`, `src/content/shop`); `src/app/index` still bundles. It needs a restart before any screen can import these modules. My files do compile under babel-preset-expo for web and iOS.\n- **Lint was not run.** ES\n\u2026(truncated; read the code/docs for the rest)\n\n### shell (lead engineer summary)\nThe app shell is in place and verified in the browser (390x844): fonts load, onboarding gate redirects to /onboarding until profile.onboardingDone, (tabs) uses expo-router/js-tabs with FloatingTabBar (Home/Academy/Coach/Shop), root Stack registers course/[id], streak, account/index, account/[section], invite, pro (modal), lesson/[id] (fullScreenModal, gestures off), story/[id] (fullScreenModal, fade), onboarding (group), dev. Root layout: font + hydration gate, useSyncTimeBasedState, settings bridge (haptics / reduce motion), web phone-width frame, <GlobalOverlays/> + <ToastHost/>.\nFiles: src/app/** are THIN re-exports of feature screens. Placeholder screens exist at src/features/{home,academy,assistant,shop,course,streak,account,invite,pro,lesson,stories,onboarding}/*-screen.tsx (they show a 'IN COSTRUZIONE' card + nav buttons) \u2014 the owning feature agent REPLACES them. src/features/dev/** holds the dev catalog (/dev, /dev/ui, /dev/icons, /dev/illustrations).\nWiring helpers: src/components/navigation/connected-status-header.tsx \u2192 <ConnectedStatusHeader onBack? stats? showAvatar? left? /> (store-connected chips; defaults: streak\u2192/streak, lives\u2192openSheet('lives'), coins\u2192/shop, avatar\u2192/account). src/components/navigation/global-overlays.tsx \u2192 OVERLAYS registry keyed by SheetName ('lives','out-of-lives','referral','rate','redeem','shield-info'), currently all null; each overlay component receives {visible,onClose}; the integrator plugs feature sheets in. It also bridges store toasts (showToast from '@/store/ui') to the kit toast (toast.show). src/lib/share.ts \u2192 shareText(message, url?, {title, copiedFeedback}) (native Share / Web Share / clipboard fallback), isShareSheetAvailable(); src/lib/clipboard.ts \u2192 copy(text) with light haptic.\nLint: eslint-config-expo installed; `npx expo lint` is clean. Typecheck clean."
const progressRule = (key) => `CHECKPOINT RULE (do this FIRST): if the file ${ROOT}/.progress/${key}.md exists, your task was already completed in an earlier run — reply with that file's exact content and do nothing else. Otherwise do the task; if some files in your folders already exist from an interrupted run, read them and continue from them instead of starting over. As your very LAST step write your final report to ${ROOT}/.progress/${key}.md (create the folder if needed) and then return the same report.\n\n`

const COMMON = `You are a senior product designer + senior mobile engineer on "Finanz" (Duolingo-style personal-finance learning app, Italian UI). Project root: ${ROOT}
The foundation is DONE. Read first: ${ROOT}/CLAUDE.md, ${ROOT}/AGENTS.md, ${ROOT}/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, ${ROOT}/docs/DESIGN_DIRECTION.md, ${ROOT}/docs/SCREEN_SPECS.md (lead-designer redlines per screen — follow them closely), ${ROOT}/docs/PRODUCT_SPEC.md (the product spec reconstructed from the reference video — feature fidelity to it is mandatory), ${ROOT}/docs/COMPONENTS.md (UI kit API — build screens ONLY from these primitives + tokens), then skim src/theme, src/components/{ui,icons,illustrations,navigation}, src/store (store API + selectors + ui store), src/content (courses, lessons, stories, shop, assistant KB), src/lib.
Foundation report (what exists, APIs, known gaps):
${FOUNDATION}
Reference frames of the original app: ${FRAMES} (read the index and open the strips for your screens with the Read tool). They are the FUNCTIONAL reference (features, flows, copy, logic). The VISUAL design must be dramatically better: playful + premium + trustworthy, top-tier consumer quality (Duolingo-level engagement/polish, Bending Spoons-level rigor), strong hierarchy, consistent spacing, tokens only (no raw hex / magic numbers outside illustrations), custom economy icons (FlameIcon/HeartIcon/KiwiCoinIcon/ShieldIcon/GemIcon…) instead of emoji for system UI, lucide for UI glyphs. Every element that is interactive in the video must be interactive here. Include loading / empty / locked / completed / error states where they make sense. Motion: fast, intentional, per src/theme/tokens/motion.ts (on web use .duration().easing() for entering/exiting — springify is ignored on web); haptics via src/lib/haptics.ts; respect reduced motion.
Environment: Node is NOT on the default PATH: run \`source "${ENV}"\` before any node/npx command. A dev server is ALREADY running on http://localhost:8081 in watch mode (do not start another). Do NOT install/remove packages or edit package.json (report needs instead). Other agents are editing other features concurrently: ONLY create/edit files you own (listed below). Placeholder screens created by the shell agent inside your feature folders are yours to replace. If you need a small change in a shared file you do not own (ui kit, store, content, theme), DO NOT edit it — work around it locally and list the requested change in your report (the integrator will apply it). Exception: you may APPEND new tokens to src/theme/tokens/* if strictly needed (never rename/remove).
Code: kebab-case files, named exports, strict TS, modular (split files > ~250 lines into components/), Italian copy in a feature-local copy.ts where it helps. Screens must work at 375×667 (iPhone SE) through 430×932, respect safe areas, floating tab bar inset (useTabBarInset) on tab screens, no horizontal overflow, 44px touch targets.
Before finishing: \`cd "${ROOT}" && npx tsc --noEmit\` — zero errors in YOUR files (ignore others' WIP). Then smoke-test that the web bundle still compiles: \`curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" "http://localhost:8081/"\` and fetch the bundle referenced by the HTML (look for the <script src=...entry.bundle...> in the HTML) — make sure it returns 200 and has no "Unable to resolve"/"SyntaxError" payload caused by your files.
Final report: files, what you implemented per screen/state, interactions, deviations from the video and why (only visual improvements, never feature removal), requested changes to shared files.`

